    {
      "title": "Deterministic Tool Execution with Typed Micro-Contracts in Agent Swarms",
      "slug": "deterministic-tool-execution-contracts",
      "excerpt": "Resolving catastrophic hallucination cascading through asynchronous schema validation and typed zero-leak contracts.",
      "content": "# Deterministic Tool Execution with Typed Micro-Contracts\n\nAutonomous agent swarms fail in enterprise deployments when tool arguments drift across unvalidated LLM turns. By placing strict Zod-style runtime constraints between agent reasoning tokens and API invocations, we guarantee zero runtime parsing exceptions.",
